This is one of the most important requirements.

The website must never invent NHS salary figures, tax rates, pension contribution rates, or payroll rules.

Use authoritative information from:

- NHS Employers.
- NHS Business Services Authority.
- NHS Pension Scheme.
- GOV.UK.
- HMRC.
- Relevant official NHS workforce and employment documentation.

Use the correct information for the applicable tax year and NHS pay framework.

Support relevant differences between:

- England.
- Wales.
- Scotland.
- Northern Ireland.

Do not assume that all UK NHS employees follow identical pay arrangements.

Where relevant, distinguish between Agenda for Change staff and medical and dental staff.

Use configurable datasets.

Every dataset must include:

- Applicable tax or financial year.
- Jurisdiction.
- Official source.
- Effective date.
- Last verified date.
- Calculation assumptions.

When official figures are unavailable, do not fabricate them.

Use a clearly labelled manual input or explain that the relevant calculation cannot yet be verified.

